{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>ואם יתקפו</b> (and if one prevail). If a single person overpowers him, the two will stand against him. The word יתקפו is among the verbs that are transitive, like תתקפהו (prevail against him). It comes deficient in nun or heh, like וזה שמו אשר יקראו. Some say the vav of יתקפו is added, but this is far-fetched: an added vav at the end of a word is not found except in nouns alone, like למעינו, מים, בנו, בעור." "<b>והחוט המשולש</b> (and a threefold cord). If the matter of 'ואין שני' (and not a second) is the helper, then 'המשולש' (the third) is the son, after the manner of לא יבשו כי ידברו את אויבים בשער."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The four examples at the end (למעינו מים בנו בעור) are listed without conjunctions in the source; read as a catalogue of nouns with final vav. בעור may be corrupt or a non-standard form.", 1 "Ibn Ezra cites Ecclesiastes 4:8 and Deuteronomy 21:5 (or similar) by fragment only; verse references resolved by context."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:37.312443144Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}